WEBVTT

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:12.530
A mail from Ovan!?

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:15.740
There is something I wish to entrust to you.

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:20.620
Come to ΔHidden Forbidden Festival.

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:00.700
Where is Haseo?

00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:02.500
Uh...

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:04.460
I think he's inside.

00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:07.920
Come on, let's go, En-sama.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:10.670
Hurry up, let's go!

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:18.470
It's that area.

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:21.140
The Serpent of Knowledge can not analysis it.

00:01:22.930 --> 00:01:23.730
Yata-sama?

00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:25.060
Interesting.

00:01:25.850 --> 00:01:26.850
That mail.

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:29.940
It looks like it wasn't a prank after all.

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:37.280
A festival?

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:46.790
This doesn't look like him.

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:54.340
Nope, it doesn't look like him.

00:02:03.350 --> 00:02:04.140
Atoli...

00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:05.310
...chan?

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:06.680
Huh?

00:02:06.980 --> 00:02:07.810
Eh...

00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:09.020
Shino-san?

00:02:09.350 --> 00:02:11.810
So Atoli-chan received that mail too.

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:12.480
Yes.

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:15.860
Eh...

00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:18.400
Has anyone else come yet?

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:21.370
There is no one else when I came here.

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:23.950
I think Haseo will be here soon.

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:26.040
Did he contact you?

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:28.410
No.

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:29.960
I just thought he would.

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:32.170
Intuition?

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:33.380
That's right.

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:34.800
A woman's intuition.

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:40.470
But if he really comes, it would seem like your hearts are connected.

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:41.840
"Connected"?

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:46.720
Someone like Shino-san suits Haseo-san better after all.

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:48.770
Why would you think that?

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:50.730
I don't have that intention.

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:52.270
Neither does Haseo.

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:54.270
Really.

00:02:55.190 --> 00:02:56.440
Don't you think so?

00:02:56.820 --> 00:03:00.700
Atoli-chan, you adventured with Haseo-san.

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:04.200
I think you can be more confident in yourself.

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:05.160
Confidence...

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:07.120
I...

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:12.210
Master, this is amazing!

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:13.960
It's a festival area!

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:15.130
Shino-san!?

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:17.050
It's Shino-san!

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:18.670
Did you change your color again?

00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:21.010
Wha...!?

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:22.390
I see two Shino-san!

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:24.260
This is Shino-san.

00:03:24.550 --> 00:03:25.390
Long time no see.

00:03:26.390 --> 00:03:29.480
It's not unusual to see the same type of PC.

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:32.310
So, why are you here?

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:34.690
I received a mail from Ovan.

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:36.650
Me too, me too!

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:39.440
So, is he here already?

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:41.400
Not yet, I think.

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:44.280
I wonder what he wants to entrust to us.

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:46.780
Is it a rare item or a treasure?

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:51.160
Or maybe he wants to restart the Twilight Brigade.

00:03:51.290 --> 00:03:52.330
No way.

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:54.210
Count me out of it.

00:03:54.580 --> 00:04:00.550
I'm tired that I still have this character, shocked that I even logged in.

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:03.300
There it is, Sakisaka's grumble!

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:06.640
So who are you?

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:07.180
Eh?

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:09.180
Why are you here?

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:10.600
Eh...

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:11.980
Yes, yes?

00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:15.810
Hey, that's more like an interrogation than a question.

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:17.270
"Interrogation"?

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:18.900
Never mind.

00:04:19.030 --> 00:04:20.860
You haven't changed a bit.

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:22.570
Not changing is number one.

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:26.870
Not changing is not the same as not growing up.

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:30.910
So you received the mail too?

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:31.450
Yes.

00:04:31.910 --> 00:04:34.460
A strange mail that mentioned nothing but the area name.

00:04:35.290 --> 00:04:36.710
Me too.

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:38.340
Why is that?

00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:43.380
We can never figure out what he is thinking.

00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:46.390
This was the case back in the Twilight Brigade days.

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:47.680
Really?

00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:52.680
If Shino-san didn't explain anything, no one would've known what to do.

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:53.810
That's true.

00:04:54.390 --> 00:04:56.480
That's the kind of person Ovan is.

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:57.270
Exactly.

00:04:57.770 --> 00:04:59.650
He never told us his objective.

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:02.280
Shino-san was his representative.

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:03.280
That's right.

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:08.280
He had a strange power to attract people.

00:05:09.620 --> 00:05:10.200
Yeah.

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:14.040
I think I understand.

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:16.210
Master, over there!

00:05:17.830 --> 00:05:19.500
There is a road over there!

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:19.750
Eh?

00:05:19.750 --> 00:05:20.750
Let's go!

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:22.130
Maybe there is treasure there.

00:05:22.670 --> 00:05:23.840
Come on, come on!

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:25.260
Uh...

00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:27.930
Tabby-san is so energetic.

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:29.930
She's like a typhoon.

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:31.600
Does she make you uncomfortable?

00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:32.470
No.

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:33.600
How should I say this...

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:37.650
It feels like there are all kinds of people around Haseo-san.

00:05:38.730 --> 00:05:39.690
You are right.

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:05.260
Speak of the devil.

00:06:05.510 --> 00:06:06.050
Huh?

00:06:06.420 --> 00:06:07.510
Who's the devil?

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:08.470
You are.

00:06:09.220 --> 00:06:10.140
What's that suppose to mean?

00:06:10.550 --> 00:06:13.640
Former members of the Twilight Brigade were here.

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:15.600
Sakisaka-kun and Tabby.

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:18.940
They went that way.

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:21.560
They are just as impulsive as always.

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:25.320
Shall we follow them?

00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:25.990
Eh?

00:06:36.750 --> 00:06:39.040
Haseo is here?

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:40.250
Are you sure?

00:06:40.710 --> 00:06:41.920
I'm sure he's around somewhere.

00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:43.880
I'm going back.

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:49.680
Huh? There are people all the way over here.

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:52.760
You are running too far ahead.

00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:57.600
But it's faster to run ahead without thinking.

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:00.810
You might miss him.

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:02.020
It's alright.

00:07:02.150 --> 00:07:03.940
There was no one who looked like Ovan.

00:07:03.980 --> 00:07:05.980
Are you guys looking for someone?

00:07:07.190 --> 00:07:10.200
We are looking for Ovan, have you seen him?

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:12.160
So he called you guys over too.

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:14.870
Ah! There is a road over here!

00:07:15.530 --> 00:07:16.410
Oh well.

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:19.750
There is something I want to tell him.

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:24.000
Come on, En-sama, let's go.

00:07:30.970 --> 00:07:32.300
It's okay.

00:07:32.970 --> 00:07:34.390
Could it be...

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:38.810
...that Ovan will come in at where we came in?

00:07:40.060 --> 00:07:43.480
Because this is a dead end.

00:07:43.850 --> 00:07:44.520
I thought so.

00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:45.650
Let's go back.

00:07:52.490 --> 00:07:55.410
Master, there is more road over here.

00:07:57.200 --> 00:07:58.370
I guess I have no choice.

00:08:00.250 --> 00:08:01.250
Welcome, welcome!

00:08:01.250 --> 00:08:02.250
Give it a try.

00:08:02.290 --> 00:08:03.540
It's delicious.

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:15.470
What's this place?

00:08:15.640 --> 00:08:16.720
What do you mean "what"?

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:17.680
It's a festival.

00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:19.970
What's Ovan thinking?

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:20.680
Who knows.

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:22.230
Don't ask me.

00:08:22.690 --> 00:08:24.850
I didn't really ask you.

00:08:26.150 --> 00:08:28.940
Now to look at it, this is really well done.

00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:31.400
But it's pointless if there is no one here.

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:32.610
I guess so.

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:34.780
How about some yakisoba?

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:35.700
Oh?

00:08:36.030 --> 00:08:37.280
Then we'll have some.

00:08:37.450 --> 00:08:39.620
There are fresh ones over there.

00:08:39.830 --> 00:08:40.620
How nice.

00:08:40.790 --> 00:08:42.040
Nice indeed.

00:08:44.250 --> 00:08:46.500
Let's wait until Ovan comes.

00:08:49.630 --> 00:08:51.210
Are you alone, miss?

00:08:51.460 --> 00:08:51.920
Hmm?

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:53.090
Who are you?

00:08:53.340 --> 00:08:54.510
What a coincidence.

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:55.930
I'm alone too.

00:08:56.340 --> 00:08:58.050
Do you know Ovan?

00:08:58.600 --> 00:09:01.140
Well, I know him more than by sight.

00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:06.350
Wait a second, miss.

00:09:07.730 --> 00:09:08.650
Would you like to join me?

00:09:13.990 --> 00:09:15.450
Another dead end?

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:21.080
You found the way?

00:09:35.420 --> 00:09:36.760
May I open it?

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:40.350
What's wrong?

00:09:40.470 --> 00:09:41.510
What's inside?

00:09:44.310 --> 00:09:45.140
Nothing...

00:09:46.230 --> 00:09:47.190
...is inside.

00:10:26.350 --> 00:10:28.060
This is the treasure?

00:10:28.190 --> 00:10:29.980
Of course not, just look at it!

00:10:35.070 --> 00:10:35.990
Are you okay?

00:10:37.860 --> 00:10:39.150
This doesn't look good.

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:40.200
Let's run, Tabby!

00:10:40.820 --> 00:10:42.410
Wait for me, master!

00:10:44.490 --> 00:10:46.080
Haseo is not here...

00:10:48.910 --> 00:10:49.870
En-sama...

00:10:50.370 --> 00:10:53.000
We are finally alone.

00:10:54.420 --> 00:10:55.250
I...

00:11:02.140 --> 00:11:03.350
En-sama...

00:11:05.310 --> 00:11:07.350
About En-sama...

00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:13.020
Run!

00:11:13.270 --> 00:11:14.730
What are you doing!?

00:11:14.770 --> 00:11:17.690
When I opened the treasure box, a shinny light went "PIKAA"!

00:11:17.740 --> 00:11:20.070
And a big shadow went "NEMOO"!

00:11:20.320 --> 00:11:23.660
Don't try to fool me with words that don't even make sense.

00:11:24.120 --> 00:11:27.910
How dare you interfere with me every time.

00:11:28.080 --> 00:11:29.410
It really went "PIKAA"!

00:11:29.460 --> 00:11:30.580
And "NEMOO"!

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:32.920
It's here!

00:11:36.920 --> 00:11:37.590
That's...

00:11:37.840 --> 00:11:38.550
It couldn't be!

00:11:39.340 --> 00:11:40.550
Master...

00:11:40.630 --> 00:11:41.720
Run...

00:11:55.900 --> 00:11:59.570
What do you all think a girl's heart is?

00:12:00.110 --> 00:12:01.530
I'll crush you.

00:12:01.700 --> 00:12:03.280
You are disturbing us.

00:12:04.700 --> 00:12:05.820
Vak Don!

00:12:17.290 --> 00:12:19.800
This is not a normal monster after all.

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:20.840
Master...

00:12:22.010 --> 00:12:22.930
En-sama...

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:26.760
Master!

00:12:41.400 --> 00:12:42.070
Haseo!

00:13:03.920 --> 00:13:05.130
This is the end.

00:13:09.850 --> 00:13:11.430
Is everyone alright?

00:13:12.140 --> 00:13:12.930
Shino-san!

00:13:22.650 --> 00:13:23.570
What?

00:13:23.780 --> 00:13:24.450
Is that...

00:13:24.900 --> 00:13:25.860
...a chim-chim?

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:26.950
Well, of course.

00:13:27.870 --> 00:13:29.320
Everyone, be careful.

00:13:29.660 --> 00:13:30.620
Wait, Haseo.

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:33.580
Shino?

00:13:38.170 --> 00:13:40.540
It looks like he has something to say.

00:13:42.630 --> 00:13:44.510
Who are you?

00:13:55.520 --> 00:13:56.270
No good.

00:13:56.640 --> 00:13:59.440
It looks like he's saying something, but I don't understand a thing.

00:13:59.980 --> 00:14:00.610
Uh...

00:14:01.150 --> 00:14:02.360
I can understand.

00:14:02.570 --> 00:14:03.320
Eh?

00:14:08.030 --> 00:14:09.240
I am...

00:14:09.740 --> 00:14:10.990
...what you call...

00:14:12.870 --> 00:14:14.830
...AIDA.

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:16.250
AIDA?

00:14:16.870 --> 00:14:19.170
Master, what's an AIDA?

00:14:19.250 --> 00:14:20.330
How would I know?

00:14:20.750 --> 00:14:23.960
All AIDA's should've been destroyed...

00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:28.720
...by Ovan's Rebirth.

00:14:39.980 --> 00:14:44.980
What was destroyed was merely the part that was not adapted to this world.

00:14:45.980 --> 00:14:46.820
He says.

00:14:47.190 --> 00:14:49.950
"The part that was not adapted to this world"?

00:14:50.740 --> 00:14:54.330
AIDA's are absorbing all the information, and evolving.

00:14:54.830 --> 00:14:57.370
Instead of attacking people like monsters,

00:14:57.700 --> 00:15:01.960
isn't it possible for them to be reborn and assimilate into game characters?

00:15:02.500 --> 00:15:03.460
Rebirth,

00:15:03.750 --> 00:15:06.590
who has the power to purify anomalies on the network.

00:15:07.170 --> 00:15:09.130
What that power didn't destroy is...

00:15:09.970 --> 00:15:13.760
It means the world has accepted AIDA, right?

00:15:16.850 --> 00:15:18.390
How am I suppose to accept that?

00:15:18.890 --> 00:15:22.860
How many players became unconscious because of them?

00:15:23.230 --> 00:15:23.900
Shino,

00:15:24.230 --> 00:15:25.020
Atoli,

00:15:25.480 --> 00:15:26.230
and Ovan!

00:15:26.860 --> 00:15:28.320
How much have you suffered?

00:15:31.820 --> 00:15:33.070
I can't forgive them.

00:15:34.160 --> 00:15:35.030
No matter what.

00:15:35.660 --> 00:15:36.870
I'll never forgive AIDA.

00:15:38.620 --> 00:15:39.540
Haseo-san...

00:15:42.420 --> 00:15:44.500
Please forgive them.

00:15:45.210 --> 00:15:45.880
Bo?

00:15:46.340 --> 00:15:48.460
They were scared.

00:15:49.050 --> 00:15:51.510
Like abandoned puppies.

00:15:52.180 --> 00:15:54.640
That's why they tried to scare everyone who got close to them.

00:15:56.010 --> 00:15:57.680
They have changed their ways.

00:15:59.140 --> 00:15:59.850
You...

00:16:00.850 --> 00:16:03.230
Hatred won't change anything.

00:16:03.650 --> 00:16:04.150
Right?

00:16:04.350 --> 00:16:07.270
Haseo nii-chan, please understand...

00:16:08.150 --> 00:16:09.690
...them.

00:16:44.940 --> 00:16:46.060
Welcome, welcome!

00:16:47.400 --> 00:16:48.770
It's open, it's open!

00:16:49.070 --> 00:16:51.030
Master, over here!

00:17:01.620 --> 00:17:02.410
Haseo.

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:04.000
Wanna try one?

00:17:05.170 --> 00:17:05.460
Sure.

00:17:09.840 --> 00:17:10.880
Alright!

00:17:11.130 --> 00:17:13.130
Mister, a hundred more times.

00:17:13.420 --> 00:17:14.630
Thanks for your business.

00:17:15.260 --> 00:17:16.430
Here I come!

00:17:18.260 --> 00:17:19.050
Haseo.

00:17:21.850 --> 00:17:22.720
Look, look.

00:17:22.890 --> 00:17:24.020
Ha-se-o!

00:17:45.410 --> 00:17:48.040
What do you think of that, Haseo?

00:17:49.080 --> 00:17:51.170
You mean the message from AIDA?

00:17:51.500 --> 00:17:52.000
Yeah.

00:17:57.510 --> 00:18:00.260
Why is it attacking us again?

00:18:04.470 --> 00:18:05.390
This is...

00:18:06.640 --> 00:18:07.600
...alphabets?

00:18:08.690 --> 00:18:09.350
R...

00:18:09.480 --> 00:18:10.110
E...

00:18:10.400 --> 00:18:10.860
T...

00:18:10.860 --> 00:18:11.320
U...

00:18:11.320 --> 00:18:12.020
R...

00:18:12.400 --> 00:18:12.980
N...

00:18:13.070 --> 00:18:13.480
E...

00:18:13.570 --> 00:18:14.150
R?

00:18:16.240 --> 00:18:17.150
Returner?

00:18:17.570 --> 00:18:19.030
Could it be that...

00:18:20.070 --> 00:18:22.530
This is what he wanted to do from the begining?

00:18:22.830 --> 00:18:23.540
It looks like it.

00:18:23.790 --> 00:18:24.330
I guess so.

00:18:28.080 --> 00:18:28.960
Returner.

00:18:29.920 --> 00:18:31.880
It means a person who has returned, right?

00:18:32.210 --> 00:18:34.210
That's not necessarily Ovan.

00:18:35.130 --> 00:18:38.010
In an area where we were summoned to by a person who addressed himself as Ovan,

00:18:38.300 --> 00:18:41.140
an AIDA came and left a message.

00:18:41.430 --> 00:18:43.180
It would be strange if they are not connected.

00:18:45.180 --> 00:18:47.680
Haseo-san, you are scared, aren't you?

00:18:49.520 --> 00:18:51.690
There is disappointment because there is expectation.

00:18:52.060 --> 00:18:54.980
Don't sound like you know everything.

00:18:55.480 --> 00:18:57.690
Now to think of it, where did you come out from?

00:18:58.780 --> 00:19:00.320
I was always here.

00:19:00.780 --> 00:19:01.240
Right?

00:19:03.240 --> 00:19:06.290
Then don't stand behind me.

00:19:06.790 --> 00:19:07.500
Hey!

00:19:07.700 --> 00:19:09.540
You looked like she guessed right.

00:19:11.580 --> 00:19:13.670
Is it really true?

00:19:15.840 --> 00:19:17.380
What are you trying to say?

00:19:17.550 --> 00:19:18.510
It's okay.

00:19:18.920 --> 00:19:21.680
Ovan won't betray your expectation.

00:19:21.970 --> 00:19:22.640
